# Provider credentials — a template.
#
# The real file lives on the VPS at $HOME/proxiapay-sandbox/provider-credentials.env,
# chmod 600, and is never committed. Every deploy seals what it holds into each
# provider account (node dist/cli/set-credentials.js); only changed values are
# re-sealed, and a provider absent from the file keeps what it has.
#
# THIS IS NOT AN ENV FILE FOR COMPOSE, and must never be passed as one. Compose
# interpolates `$`, so a secret containing one would be silently truncated. The
# CLI parses this file itself, literally: write values exactly as issued.
#
# Names are mechanical — the provider code, then the key the adapter reads:
# `ejara` + `clientKey` = EJARA_CLIENT_KEY. A name the adapter would not read
# (EJARA_CLIENT_ID, say) is refused and the deploy fails, rather than storing a
# credential the adapter would send as an empty value.

# Ejara Pay — for the account pointed at the prodbox. Ejara calls the first value
# a client id in places; it is the client KEY here.
EJARA_CLIENT_KEY=<client key>
EJARA_CLIENT_SECRET=<client secret>
